  "findings": [
    "Stage 56 is the final checkpoint in the old derivative, so the reported screen does not locate a stall after ramoops.",
    "CDC has a real strong BL in bsd_init after IOKitInitializeTime; its call is substantially later than the bounded arm_init region.",
    "The initial boot thread template already exists from thread_bootstrap, but kernel_bootstrap has not yet created or switched to the scheduled bootstrap thread. The boot CPU reaches machine_startup first; kernel_thread_create and load_context occur later inside kernel_bootstrap.",
    "fiq_context_init actual code reads DAIF and asserts masked A/I/F bits, writes CNTV_CTL_EL0=1 and CNTP_CTL_EL0=2; it does not unmask DAIF.",
    "PE_init_platform(TRUE) maps interrupt/timer registers and initializes timebase data, but does not itself unmask CPU DAIF or schedule.",
    "The built-in pe_init_fiq is BTI c; RET in this actual input. This proves HAS_GIC_V3 built-in code was not selected, not that every GIC provider is missing: the recorded actual link also force-loads the separate ArmCpu archive.",
    "The no-return machine_startup wrapper may report entry and then set LR=original BL site+4 followed by B to the original callee. It must not invent an after-return stage.",
    "No hardware cause for the missing USB port is established by this audit; expanded checkpoints distinguish earlier execution paths only."
  ],
